From 3d8e2411205adc8938fbf81a6d24a159542f9cce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:22:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] Fair admission between concurrent playback readers

Waiting playback requests took freed download slots strictly in arrival order,
so a stream with a deep read-ahead queue held a second stream's reads behind its
whole window: on a loopback provider with 4 connections at 4 MB/s, a stream
opened 0.5 s after another got 20% of the throughput. Probe now carries the
reader's id, and a freed slot goes to the waiting playback request of the
reader holding the fewest slots, oldest first. The late stream now gets 40-43%.
Background admission and the heavy-waiter rule are unchanged.
